--- !u!114 &212369657
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 212369656}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: bd8247e9fc96a7f4c95b91b320ab5883, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NpcDialogue
  storyStates:
  - minimumStoryBeat: 4
    location: {fileID: 1238231649}
    spriteOverride: {fileID: 0}
    overrideSortingOrder: 0
    sortingOrder: 0
    isVisible: 1
    isInteractable: 1
    lines:
    - speaker: Cyrus
      text: Alan says he started today.
    - speaker: Cyrus
      text: Janet thinks she's been here for months.
    - speaker: Cyrus
      text: Their files say years.
    - speaker: Cyrus
      text: And so does mine.
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: Not everyone loses the same amount.
    - speaker: Cyrus
      text: Loses?
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: Retains, if you'd prefer.
    - speaker: Cyrus
      text: I wouldn't.
    - speaker: Cyrus
      text: The camera. The files. The logs.
    - speaker: Cyrus
      text: The way people talk, then stop themselves.
    - speaker: Cyrus
      text: The way they look at me like I'm supposed to know something.
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: And now you do.
    - speaker: Cyrus
      text: I know enough to know that something's missing.
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: 'That''s usually where this starts. '
    - speaker: Cyrus
      text: Usually?
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: 'Sometimes it''s the camera first. Sometimes the logs. '
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: Today was cleaner than most.
    - speaker: Cyrus
      text: Cleaner?
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: You got here before anyone else started asking the same questions.
    - speaker: Cyrus
      text: So that's what this is about? Keeping everyone quiet?
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: Keeping the work intact.
    - speaker: Cyrus
      text: The work..
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: 'In seven years, this floor has answered questions people have spent
        fifty years circling. '
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: There are treatments in use now because of it.
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: 'Not theories. Not papers. Treatments. '
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: People who were disappearing by inches are still present because someone
        here kept recording what others couldn't.
    - speaker: Cyrus
      text: And that makes this acceptable?
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: 'It makes it harder. '
    - speaker: Cyrus
      text: They never agreed to this.
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: No, they didn't.
    - speaker: Cyrus
      text: Did I?
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: Not in any way that would comfort you.
    - speaker: Cyrus
      text: That's not an answer.
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: No, but it's the one you usually accept.
    - speaker: Cyrus
      text: Did I agree to this?
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: Once, you wanted the truth preserved at any cost.
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: Then we learned what any cost meant.
    - speaker: Cyrus
      text: 'I don''t remember wanting that. '
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: 'That''s the mercy, and the problem. '
    - speaker: Cyrus
      text: So what happens now?
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: Usually?
    - speaker: Cyrus
      text: Usually.
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: You ask whether I'm going to stop you.
    - speaker: Cyrus
      text: And are you?
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: Not unless you make it necessary.
    - speaker: Cyrus
      text: Why?
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: Because coercion ruins the data.
    - speaker: Cyrus
      text: Data? I'm not one of your patients.
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: No.
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: Patients are treated. You are measured.
    - speaker: Cyrus
      text: So that's why you're letting me choose?
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: 'The meal or the call. Yes. '
    - speaker: Cyrus
      text: Does the call even go anywhere?
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: It rings.
    - speaker: Cyrus
      text: That's not what I asked.
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: No, but it's what you get before choosing.
    - speaker: Cyrus
      text: And after?
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: The record continues either way.
    repeatLines:
    - speaker: Cyrus
      text: You're just going to wait?
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: I'm going to observe.
    storyBeatAfterDialogue: 5
  - minimumStoryBeat: 0
    location: {fileID: 1501422207}
    spriteOverride: {fileID: 0}
    overrideSortingOrder: 0
    sortingOrder: 0
    isVisible: 1
    isInteractable: 1
    lines:
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: Ah! There you are. Welcome to our little corner of the Helix Facility.
        I'm Director Pryce.
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: I'll keep this brief - your role here is very straightforward.
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: Patrol your routes, check the exits are secure, and most importantly,
        ensure that nothing disrupts the work.
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: The research we do here is important. More important than most people
        will ever understand.
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: ...or even acknowledge...
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: You just need to make sure it continues!
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: The staff here are extremely committed to the work, but that doesn't
        mean you won't find them pleasant. So don't let them distract you from your
        responsibilities.
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: If you have any concerns, come directly to me. Not to the researchers,
        not to the staff. Me.
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: Your route is standard, so you shouldn't have any issues. And the canteen
        is open if you need it.
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: Before you start, open your task board with TAB. It contains your patrol
        route and current assignment.
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: When you reach a task, press E to interact with it.
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: If you lose track of what you're doing, press TAB again to review the
        list.
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: Now, go on. We've already spent far too long yapping about. We've got
        science to do.
    repeatLines:
    - speaker: Pryce
      text: The board has your tasks. Get a move on.
    storyBeatAfterDialogue: 0
  useScenePlacementForInitialState: 1
