    machineStatus: Normal
    notes: Routine distribution completed through staff meal cycle. Personnel were
      not briefed, per Protocol E restrictions. Intake remained within expected range.
      No recall events observed after previous service.
  - title: Daily Reports
    entry: C-120
    date: 02/03/1971
    system: HX-7B Dietary Distribution
    area: Floor C  - Long Term Retention
    doseCycle: Evening Meal Service
    batch: HX-7B-44
    machineStatus: Minor pressure variance
    notes: One security subject missed scheduled intake due to route deviation. Subject
      displayed increased questioning and attempted unscheduled conversation with
      kitchen staff. Reintegration through next meal service required.
  - title: Daily Reports
    entry: C-121
    date: 03/03/1971
    system: HX-7B Dietary Distribution
    area: Floor C  - Long Term Retention
    doseCycle: Evening Meal Service
    batch: HX-7B-44
    machineStatus: Dispenser fault
    notes: Automated dosage failed for multiple assigned personnel. Exposure group
      may experience memory overlap, identity fixation, and resistance to posted
      duties. Personnel are to remain in designated areas until intake schedule is
      restored.
  - title: Daily Reports
    entry: C-122
    date: 04/03/1971
    system: HX-7B Dietary Distribution
    area: Floor C  - Long Term Retention
    doseCycle: Evening Meal Service
    batch: HX-7B-44
    machineStatus: Offline
    notes: Long-term exposure records confirm continued service across multiple induction
      resets. Affected personnel continue to identify current assignment as recent
      when dosage is maintained. One subject has displayed partial continuity between
      resets and appears to be leaving prompts for other long-term personnel across
      repeated induction cycles.
  - title: Daily Reports
    entry: C-123
    date: 05/03/1971
    system: HX-7B Dietary Distribution
    area: Floor C  - Long Term Retention
    doseCycle: Evening Meal Service
    batch: HX-7B-44
    machineStatus: Offline
    notes: Sustained questioning after missed intake should be documented before
      correction. Direct interruption may compromise behavioural record. If external
      escalation is attempted, administration is to be notified before outgoing contact
      is made. Route removal authorised only if breach becomes unavoidable.
  minimumStoryBeatToInteract: 3
  storyBeatAfterFirstOpen: 4
  minimumStoryBeatToAdvance: 3
  onlyAdvanceStory: 1
